No verified public benchmark numbers (SWE-bench Pro, Terminal-Bench, GPQA/HLE, AA Index, etc.) for this exact model/ID were found in this research pass. Per `tasks/research.md` rule 9 and `RULES.md`, this file is saved as `DeepSeek_4_Flash.md.excluded` (notes only, never counted) instead of a fabricated scored report.

- OpenAI's "Introducing GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark" post (2026-02-12) states it is a smaller, real-time-optimized GPT-5.3-Codex variant running on Cerebras WSE-3 at >1000 tokens/s, but reports its SWE-Bench Pro and Terminal-Bench 2.0 results only as charts with no numeric values in the text.
- Verified non-benchmark facts: research preview for ChatGPT Pro (+ API design partners); 128K context window; text-only; minimal-edit default working style.
- No first-party or third-party (Artificial Analysis, BenchLM) numeric benchmark rows for the exact ID were located; Artificial Analysis has no page for it.
- Re-research trigger: if numeric SWE-Bench Pro / Terminal-Bench / AA Index results are published for GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark, write a fresh `DeepSeek_4_Flash.md` and retire this twin.

